WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.540
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.140
Labor X-10, Out of Control

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.790
It's beautiful!

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.120
I'm so glad we came, Mamoru!

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.590
The autumn leaves are
so beautiful!

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.590
Your lips are more beautiful.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.840
Mamoru!

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.610
What's that Labor
doing here?

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.990
Special Vehicles,
Second Section.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.450
Yes, speaking.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.120
At Gotenba?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.130
National Route 138?

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:07.560
The first horse in race 2
weighs in at under 2 kilograms.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:14.310
Yes, I understand.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.280
Is there some point to this?

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.830
We get bigger tomatoes
if I pinch off some of the buds.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.370
Hiromi, why did you
become a policeman?

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.380
You're more suited to
farming than fighting Labors.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:44.220
I mean, ah, you could probably
take on a Labor barehanded!

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.060
Division 2,
emergency mobilization.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.430
Division 2,
emergency mobilization.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:02.150
Captain!
I have lots of questions!

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.240
I imagine so.
I haven't told you much...

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.120
only that we're being sent
to the Gotenba Interchange.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.410
This is an emergency,
isn't it?

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.290
Yes.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:21.000
So shouldn't we have our
sirens on, to get there quickly?

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.720
I agree!
We need to make more noise!

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.720
But if headquarters wanted
us to move discreetly...

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:34.230
they'd simply ask for
a rapid mobilization.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:40.360
Exactly. This time,
I'm in the same boat you are.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.320
The same boat?

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:47.820
All I know is that I was told to
go to the Gotenba Interchange...

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.780
enter National Route 138,
and wait for contact.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.330
Good to see you. I'm Aogi
of the prefectural police.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.120
Goto, Special Vehicles,
Second Section.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.420
What are the
roadblocks for?

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.540
I don't know.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:28.210
We've been ordered to
close off National Route 138.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.680
So you got orders, too?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:31.970
What's going on?

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.680
I have a bad
feeling about this.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:41.020
But since we were sent,
it must involve Labors.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.190
Like what?

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.400
We'll find out, soon enough.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.490
Have you discovered anything,
Shinobu?

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.110
I've checked everywhere,
but no.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:59.330
Is HQ keeping quiet, or are
they out of the loop on this?

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:05.920
Everything is sealed off around
Lake Yamanaka and Route 138...

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.960
but the explanation
is strange.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:08.460
Strange?

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:13.470
Traffic reports say the roads
were closed due to large cracks.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.550
Around Kagozaka
Pass, near Lake Yamanaka.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:18.680
Cracks in the road?

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:22.350
I hope they don't want to use
our Ingrams for highway work!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.850
I'll call you
if I learn anything else.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.770
Thanks for your help.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.940
The story about
cracks is strange.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:35.160
We came from Lake
Yamanaka just two hours ago.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.870
We didn't see any problems.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.370
How about
Kagozaka Pass?

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.700
We had no problems
there, either.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.370
Two hours ago...

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:47.670
Captain, we were ordered
to mobilize before that.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.210
What does it mean?

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:54.090
All I can say is that they're
trying to pursue this secretly...

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.640
and it's near Lake
Yamanaka, whatever it is.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.500
Squad 3 has
broken through.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:35.340
The X10 has changed course.
It's heading toward Yamanaka.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.180
We've just hit our
worst-case scenario.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.180
The X10 is intended to
be an unmanned unit...

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:48.810
so it's equipped with the
latest in artificial intelligence.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.730
Unfortunately, we seem
to have lost control...

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.030
and its program
includes leveling a city.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:58.110
You mean that thing
is heading for a city?

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.910
No, we didn't load a
map into its database...

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:05.500
so it doesn't have
a target yet. However...

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.290
However?

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:11.290
To find a city to level, it's
programmed to follow the roads.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.800
It will soon reach
National Route 138...

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:19.220
and that should lead it
straight to Gotenba, here.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.720
The government has already
called in the metropolitan police.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:28.600
Any further moves on our
part might look VERY bad.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.940
Let's hope
they can handle it.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:36.860
They'd better be able to stop
it before the contact point.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.690
Ground Defense Force Model 97

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.510
Goto here.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:48.560
What's your location?

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.230
National Route 138,
just outside Gotenba.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.440
Good.
Here's your mission...

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:05.530
Stop a runaway Labor?
Why can't it stop on its own?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:10.660
Good question.
Also consider this fact...

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:15.880
It will detect other Labors on
its sensors and attack them.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.380
What?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:22.050
Wait a minute. You said,
"On its sensors."

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:25.800
Are you saying
this thing is unmanned?

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:26.600
So it would seem.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:31.430
A Labor isn't usually
equipped with weapons...

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.560
unless it's...

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:34.900
A military Labor.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.820
Yeah, everything fits.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:43.860
And the military has a practice
range at the base of Mount Fuji.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:47.280
But if the Self Defense
Force has a runaway Labor...

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.620
why don't they deal with it?

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.330
They tried and failed.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.910
The JSDF told you that?

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:58.090
No, but remember that
we were on standby alert.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:03.670
It seems likely that
we were stage 2 of their plan.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.130
Stage 2?

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:10.970
If they could handle it, they'd
just send us back to the station.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.270
I don't want the blame
for a military screw-up.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.900
You only give me orders.
I'M the one who'll get the blame.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:20.360
How vulgar.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.750
Why haven't we heard anything
more on that runaway Labor?

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.420
We're linked to the
Prefectural Police, but...

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.130
Captain, headquarters
just called!

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.880
Halt! Halt!

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.270
Stop or I'll shoot!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.330
Yamanashi
to headquarters.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.040
The runaway Labor has
broken through at Yamanaka.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.460
It's moving up National
Route 138, toward Gotenba.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.380
It must be stopped!

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:27.550
Roger.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.260
Well, then.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.190
This might be a
convenient place to do it.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.560
Time for work.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.900
We'll wait for it here.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.490
We'll lure it into
this construction site.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.240
Remember,
this won't be a walk in the park.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.330
Roger!

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.040
Noa, stand by!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:57.620
I'm ready whenever.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.710
Labor carrier, deck up!

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:00.580
Roger.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.610
It might try to shoot
from back there.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.570
I'll kill it!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:10.490
Here it comes!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.410
Target verified!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.870
What's with the paint job?

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.000
It doesn't look
like a military Labor.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.880
Noa, hurry up!

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:25.920
Roger.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.050
I don't want to
hit him head-on!

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.350
Noa, now!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:55.200
It's coming!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.130
Good work.
Make it use up its ammo.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.880
Easy for you to say!

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.430
Submit!

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:21.350
Ota, pick your
shots more carefully!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:22.980
I'm the one stopping it!

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:24.600
And I'm the one
giving orders!

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.240
Are you okay, Ota?

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:56.840
That proves it.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.390
Look on the Labor's hull.
They tried to cover it over.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:06.850
It says "X-10."
That means...

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.900
It's an experimental unit.

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:12.940
So it's a secret military project...

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:18.320
and now the thing's
running wild.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.370
The entire project's
probably top secret...

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:26.500
because the media would
have a field day with this.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.420
That's a dangerous toy
to lose control of.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.210
Damn!
I'm out of bullets!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.550
What did you plan to do
if you ran out of ammo first?

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:41.220
Ota!

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.310
Noa!

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:06.750
It's out of ammo! Noa,
close in and go for its legs!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:07.950
Roger!

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:17.510
Don't hesitate!

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:18.630
But...

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.380
I'll do it!

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.390
What happened?

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.940
Don't worry,
it's just a smoke bomb!

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.530
Where is it?
I can't see a thing!

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.320
It's jumping!

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:53.580
Izumi, now!

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:54.920
Okay!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:02.880
This thing's really tough.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.930
We can't overpower it.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.930
Captain, it's stronger
than our Labors.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:12.520
I think someone needs
to get aboard to stop it.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.440
That's just
what I was thinking.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:17.860
You do it, Shinohara.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.650
Me?

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:22.150
Is anyone else qualified?

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:26.780
I know you can do it,
Asuma. Good luck!

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:36.210
Hurry up, Izumi!

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.670
Be careful!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.130
I know.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:46.800
Are you trying
to kill me?

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.930
I'm doing my best!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:54.980
The motors in the Ingrams
are at their limit. Hurry!

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:58.940
I can't hold on
here forever!

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.400
I'm past my limit!

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.870
Asuma, are you okay?

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:10.910
Somehow.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:15.670
Here it is!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:19.670
Asuma!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.380
I'm busy!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.510
Where's the disc?
Here?

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:31.720
Asuma, stop it!

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.340
I'm exhausted!

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:12.930
I could've stopped it sooner,
if I'd had more bullets!

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:16.560
What are you saying?
At the end, you almost fainted!

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:18.400
Now THAT was a tough job.

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:22.980
But I feel kind of sorry
for that poor Labor.

00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:27.030
Captain, was it wise to leave
an experimental military Labor...

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:29.450
just sitting in the
middle of a vacant lot?

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.950
Weren't we ordered to destroy it
and deny any involvement?

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:36.410
Well, it was too tough
to be destroyed anyway.

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:45.840
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:49.550
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:55.810
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:05.320
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:08.240
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:12.820
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:17.500
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:20.330
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:24.500
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:31.010
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:36.260
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.810
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:42.020
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:46.110
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:52.280
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:58.330
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:04.960
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.470
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.470
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:17.680
"The Tower" is an
imposing new structure...

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:19.810
once complete it will be
1000 meters high.

00:24:20.100 --> 00:24:22.020
Someone's started a fire
at about 200 meters...

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.440
and an ambassador's
trapped inside!

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:26.940
The Fire Department's Labors
failed their rescue!

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:29.440
The only hope left is
two of our Ingrams.

00:24:29.820 --> 00:24:32.030
Do you think Captain
Goto's plan will work?

00:24:32.530 --> 00:24:34.910
Next Episode:
"The Tower: S.O.S."

00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:36.870
Target, Lock On!

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:41.500
Next episode

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:41.500
The Tower: S.O.S.
